# A-Multilayer-Visibility-Graph-Framework-for-Ultrashort-Term-Analysis
## ROSSLER

## HYPOL

## EDA SENSING 
### EDA Preprocessing
- main1_eda_cveda.m: the routine used the cvx eda function to extract the pahis, tonic and SMNA component of the EDA signal
### EDA visbility graph
#### Real dyads
1. cut_signal_for_esgo_eda.m : The routine cuts SMNA signlas in 60s and1 180s windows. It also resample it at 4 Hz and save all the segments (sampled and not) in  a mat structure.
2. VG_EDA_trainer_trainee.m : The routine uses the mat structure file generateb by cut_signal_fors_esgo_eda-m to calculate each partecipant single layer, duplex trainer trainee VG,duplex VG of partecipants belonging to the same couple
#### Surrogates
1. create_surrogates_tables.m : % This routine splits the EDA SMNA signal windows saved in the previous step (cust_signal_for_esgo_eda.m) into trainer and trainee tables. The tables contain the 60 s and 180 s windows into which the signal was previously divided. These tables will be used to create the homogeneous and non-homogeneous surrogates in the following routine, surrogate_shuffled.m.
2. surrogates_shuffled.m:% This routine creates the homologous and non-homologous surrogates. It uses as input the trainer and trainee tables generated by create_surrogate_tables.m. The script generates the surrogates by shuffling the trainee windows with those of trainers who did not participate in the same session.
3. esportazione_r_all_surr_libra
